{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2021-10-07 13:00:00', 'title': "PG&E'S WEATHER WEBPAGE PROVIDES CUSTOMERS WITH LATEST METEOROLOGICAL INFORMATION IN THEIR COMMUNITY, GAUGES PUBLIC SAFETY POWER SHUTOFF POTENTIAL", 'text': 'SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--AS PART OF ITS EFFORTS TO PREPARE CUSTOMERS AND COMMUNITIES FOR THE GROWING THREAT OF WILDFIRES, PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E) IS PROVIDING DETAILED, LOCALIZED WEATHER FORECASTS FOR CUSTOMERS FROM ITS ROBUST WEATHER WEBPAGE ON PGE.COM. THE WEATHER WEBPAGE OFFERS A SEVEN-DAY FORECAST UPDATED DAILY BY A PG&E METEOROLOGIST OR FIRE SCIENTIST THAT INDICATES THE POTENTIAL NEED TO CALL A PUBLIC SAFETY POWER SHUTOFF (PSPS). PG&E MONITORS CONDITIONS'}